{
  "mn76:0.1": "Middle Discourses 76 ",
  "mn76:0.2": "With Sandaka ",
  "mn76:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn76:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Kosambī in Ghosita’s monastery. ",
  "mn76:2.1": "Now at that time the wanderer Sandaka was residing at the cave of the wavy leaf fig tree together with a large assembly of around five hundred wanderers. ",
  "mn76:3.1": "Then in the late afternoon, Venerable Ānanda came out of retreat and addressed the mendicants: ",
  "mn76:3.2": "“Come, reverends, let’s go to the Devakata Pool to see the cave.” ",
  "mn76:3.3": "“Yes, reverend,” they replied. ",
  "mn76:3.4": "Then Ānanda together with several mendicants went to the Devakata Pool. ",
  "mn76:4.1": "Now at that time, Sandaka and the large assembly of wanderers were sitting together making an uproar, a colossal racket. They engaged in all kinds of low talk, such as ",
  "mn76:4.2": "talk about kings, bandits, and chief ministers; talk about armies, threats, and wars; talk about food, drink, clothes, and beds; talk about garlands and fragrances; talk about family, vehicles, villages, towns, cities, and countries; talk about women and heroes; talk at the street market and the place for water pots; talk about the departed; motley talk; tales of land and sea; and talk about being reborn in this or that place. ",
  "mn76:4.3": "Sandaka saw Ānanda coming off in the distance, ",
  "mn76:4.4": "and hushed his own assembly, ",
  "mn76:4.5": "“Be quiet, good fellows, don’t make a sound. ",
 